// Algorithm: Ticket Trace

1. Read N and repeat until it is between 5 and 15.
2. Read the N ticket IDs, repeating each one until it is between 1 and N.
3. Print the scan sequence.
4. For each ID from 1 to N, count how many times it appears in the log.
5. If an ID's count is 0, mark it as missing; if its count is 2, mark it as the duplicate.
6. If there is not exactly one missing ID and one duplicate, print "Invalid scan log" and stop.
7. Print the duplicate ID and the missing ID.
8. For each position i, compare ticket[i] with every ticket to its right, and count it when ticket[i] is bigger.
9. Print the out-of-order pair count.
10. Read R and calculate target = (R % N) + 1.
11. Scan the log and print every position (counted from 1) where the ticket equals the target.
12. Print the target ID and its occurrence count.
